From: Orion <orionopenwow@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] openvanilla: Duels hosted rooms (a player's own duel world, with a link for friends)

Owner, 2026-10-22: "people host their own duel worlds and give a link to friends", run on our server, the
host choosing the mode and rules and who can join. A room is a private duel world inside the Duels realm:
a 6-letter code (duels.openvanilla.app/?room=CODE), the host's mode (1v1 rated rules off, practice,
2v2, 3v3), best of 1/3/5, sudden death on or off, betting on or off, and who may join (link, public,
password). Its members queue among themselves ("join room"); its matches are unrated, each in its own
copy of the arena like every match, and feed the room's own ladder. No extra world server per room:
up to 50 open rooms, 40 players each; empty rooms close after 30 minutes; a restart closes them all.
The public rooms go to duels_now row 2 for the website's "Join a server". See the Command comments.

